CS:GO world-model recording showing a first-person weapon and a stone courtyard","alt","Recording type","Original project recording","role","provenance","Track","World models","track","metadata","Related project",[91],"resourceId",{"_49":92,"_26":93},"DIAMOND — Diffusion for World Modeling","/resources/diamond/","What this recording shows","This is neural prediction of game frames, not the CS:GO engine or a complete source game. The original recording is 280×150 pixels and visibly soft. Public local world-model play requires the released code, checkpoints, and suitable hardware.","limitations","Demo category","World model","demoType","lead","world","world-model","source-recording","recordingId","diamond","resource:diamond","resource","Trains reinforcement learning agents inside diffusion world models that preserve visual detail.","/resources/",{"_20":105,"_178":92,"_176":101,"_47":179,"_177":108,"_172":171,"_26":169,"_57":180,"_155":181,"_151":182,"_146":183,"_140":184,"_137":136},[113,114,115,116,117,118,119,120,121,122,123,124,125,126],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_47":22,"_51":92,"_53":178,"_55":-7},{"_47":100,"_51":108,"_53":177,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":175,"_51":85,"_53":176,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":173,"_51":174,"_53":47,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":170,"_51":171,"_53":172,"_55":56},{"_47":57,"_49":166,"_59":167,"_53":26,"_55":-7},{"_47":57,"_49":162,"_59":163,"_53":57,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":153,"_143":144,"_59":154,"_53":155,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":149,"_143":144,"_59":150,"_53":151,"_55":-7},{"_47":141,"_49":142,"_143":144,"_59":145,"_53":146,"_55":-7},{"_47":48,"_49":138,"_51":139,"_53":140,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_49":135,"_51":136,"_53":137,"_55":87},{"_47":48,"_53":132,"_49":133,"_51":134},{"_47":57,"_53":127,"_49":128,"_59":129},"identitySource","Identity evidence",[130],{"_49":131,"_26":63},"University of Geneva","identity","Identity & attribution","The project page lists equal-contribution first authors Eloi Alonso (University of Geneva) and Adam Jelley (University of Edinburgh), with Microsoft Research also involved. Select the first author’s first institution, Geneva. The SVG is from the official university homepage and was provided/verified by the root agent.","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","Year","2024","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[147,148,85],"dimensions","2D","3D","Development stages",[152,85],"stages","Testing","Topics",[156,157,158,159,160,161],"tags","neural-simulator","interactive-video","diffusion","Atari","reinforcement-learning","NeurIPS-2024","Further reading",[164],{"_49":165,"_26":63},"Code and playable models","Project source",[168],{"_49":166,"_26":169},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399","Why it belongs here","Visual Details Matter in Atari studies diffusion models as environment models in which agents learn from imagined trajectories, analyzing how visual detail affects policies. Alongside the Atari 100k evaluation, the paper trains a playable neural engine on prerecorded CS:GO gameplay. It is relevant to simulation, control, and accumulated prediction error.","detail","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","summary","name","paper",[188],[156,157,158,159,160,161],[187,101],[185,186,101],2024,"2d","3d","test",{"_49":165,"_26":63},{"_190":191},"documents",{"_192":193,"_194":195},"en",[197,201,202,203,200,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221,222,223,224,225,226,227,228,229,230,231,232,233,234,235,199,236,198,237,238,239,240,241,242,243,244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254,255,256,257],"zh",[196,197,198,199,200],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","prod